   "design": "Suppliers send bills to an invoice inbox that reads them into the accounting system. Each bill is matched against the booking and the supplier's confirmation in the booking system, and only differences come to the guide, who checks the bills before they are booked. Due bills make up a payment batch, which the guide checks and releases to the bank. The bank feed records payments, replacing the cash book. Supplier calls about wrong bills stay with the guide.",
   "previous_blocker": "Bills were collected, matched, typed and recorded by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Invoice inboxes, booking-linked matching and bank feeds.",
   "still_hard": "Small local suppliers who want cash.",
   "human_edge": "Knowing which supplier to call before a bill becomes a problem.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Most typing and matching disappear; the release and supplier talks stay.",
